WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.150 --> 00:00:04.360
AGV: Today we're talking about
data stream, artifact registry,

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:05.890
and API design.

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:08.710
I'm AGV, and welcome to "This
Week in Cloud," where we serve

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:10.960
you the lowest latency news.

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:13.540
On top of all the data
announcements from last week,

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.149
we've also launched
Data Stream in preview.

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:18.610
Data Stream is a serverless
change data capture

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:21.520
and replication service that
allows you to synchronize data

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:25.270
across databases,
storage, and applications.

00:00:25.270 --> 00:00:27.700
Creating a stream
captures data changes

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:29.740
from sources like
Oracle and MySQL

00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:32.350
and stores it in
cloud storage where

00:00:32.350 --> 00:00:35.140
you can use Dataflow to
transform the data to however

00:00:35.140 --> 00:00:35.710
you need.

00:00:35.710 --> 00:00:38.530
Try it out today, and stay
tuned for even more supported

00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:40.580
data sources soon.

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:42.680
As a developer, you
need a secure place

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:44.180
to store all your stuff--

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:46.160
container images, of course--

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:49.100
but also language packages
that can enable code

00:00:49.100 --> 00:00:51.740
reuse across multiple
applications.

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:53.510
Today, we're pleased
to announce support

00:00:53.510 --> 00:00:57.440
for Node.js, Python, and Java
repositories for artifact

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:58.910
registry in preview.

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:01.730
Now you can not only secure and
distribute container images,

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:06.220
but also manage and secure
your other software artifacts.

00:01:06.220 --> 00:01:09.370
If you're looking to develop,
run, and secure applications

00:01:09.370 --> 00:01:12.160
across your hybrid and
multi-cloud environments,

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:14.560
look no further than Anthos.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:17.050
And to learn more about
this managed platform

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:20.380
and how it can help you, check
out the Anthos 101 learning

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.970
series, all Anthos--

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:23.910
all in one spot.

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:27.660
APIs play a critical role
in helping software connect

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:31.050
and communicate as well as
making the lives of developers

00:01:31.050 --> 00:01:32.430
a little easier.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:35.430
And to make it easier
for you to use them,

00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:38.790
we've compiled a list of
our most popular posts.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:40.980
Head over to the blog for more.

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:43.680
If you want to read more about
any of these announcements

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:46.390
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:46.390 --> 00:01:47.910
Any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:49.660
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:51.830
We'll see you in the cloud.

